body:
```suggestion
	godot_js_os_pthread_pool_size_get: function () {
		if (typeof PThread === 'undefined') {
		    // Threads aren't supported, so default to `1`.
			return 1;
		}
		const total = PThread.runningWorkers.length + PThread.unusedWorkers.length;
		return Math.max(1, total - 1);
	},
```

- I think we should always prefer early exiting.
- `if (PThread == null)` could be valid too, but I'm not _that_ nitpicky.

It seems that you can trust that `Pthread.{runningWorkers,unusedWorkers}` exist. I didn't see anything [in the emscripten source code](https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/) that suggests that these could be anything else than arrays.

